#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203803 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/id #uuid "6f0e3d4b-943b-5710-a996-ac4d3c68778d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16399" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n\nCalculate $S_{xy}$." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n}$, $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their respective means, that is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{xy} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sample means $\\overline{x}$ and $\\overline{y}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{15+12+13+16+19}{5} = 15\n$$\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{8+13+6+15+13}{5} = 11\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the differences between the $x_i$ and $\\overline{x}$, $y_i$ and $\\overline{y}$, and their product.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $13$ | $16$ | $19$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $8$ | $13$ | $6$ | $15$ | $13$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| **$\\, (y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $-3$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n| **$\\, (x_i - \\overline{x})(y_i - \\overline{y}) \\,$** | $0$ | $-6$ | $10$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n\nTherefore, $S_{xy}$ is\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = 0 + (-6) + 10 + 4 + 8 = 16\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203804 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83df73fc-c0cc-5605-9b39-453de0c37cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating S(x,y) Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "489e5ffd-9e78-567b-b009-25d0c004825a" :question/math-academy-id "e-16400" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $30$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{30}$, and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{30}$. You are given that\n$∑_(i = 1)^(30)x_{i} = 315,; ∑_(i = 1)^(30)y_{i} = 278,; ∑_(i = 1)^(30)x_{i}y_{i} = 2964$.\nDetermine $S_{xy}$." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n}$, the statistic $S_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{xy} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)) \\\\\n&= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}y_{i} - \\frac{1}{n}(∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i})(∑_(i = 1)^(n)y_{i})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{xy} &= 2964 - \\frac{1}{30}(315)(278) \\\\\n&= 2964 - 2919 \\\\\n&= 45\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203805 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "714000f9-caea-57a3-a8cb-6b8ec99960d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Variance and Covariance"}] :question/id #uuid "7daa2313-4672-5624-aac2-e3b87b6ec366" :question/math-academy-id "e-16401" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $35$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{35}$, and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{35}$. You are given that\n$S_{xx} = 35, S_{yy} = 133, S_{xy} = 105$.\n\nWhat is the value of $\\mathrm{Cov}(x, y)$?" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n}$, their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov(x, y) &= \\frac{S_{xy}}{n}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $S_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of $x_i$ and $y_i$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nS_{xy} = 105\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nCov(x, y) &= \\frac{105}{35} \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203806 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f0ed04b-f011-5818-952d-425a19e0cd5c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Using the Shortcut Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "9804df95-f494-5d99-acbd-97c69344d401" :question/math-academy-id "e-16402" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\, x_i \\,$** | $10$ | $9$ | $8$ | $8$ | $5$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **$\\, y_i \\,$** | $15$ | $12$ | $14$ | $12$ | $8$ |\n\nGiven that $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334$, calculate $S_{xx}$." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \\ldots, x_{n}$ and $y_{1}, y_2, \\ldots, y_{n}$, the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data $x_i$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{xx} &= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2} \\\\\n&= ∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i}^{2} - \\frac{1}{n}(∑_(i = 1)^(n)x_{i})^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the $x_i$ data:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n x_i = 10 + 9 + 8 + 8 + 5 = 40\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^5 x_i^2 = 334\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\nS_{xx} =334 - \\dfrac{1}{5}(40)^2 = 334- 320 = 14\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204443 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "67543802-7a9b-5136-8b6c-fb241a29ee8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202599}] :question/id #uuid "afc7ddce-cfae-538b-a2da-388062ae3528" :question/math-academy-id "q-251486" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $8$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_{2}, …, x_{8}$, and $y_{1}, y_{2}, …, y_{8}$.\n\nYou are given that\n$∑_(i = 1)^(8)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2} = 1.6,; ∑_(i = 1)^(8)(y_{i} - y^(―))^{2} = 5.1,; ∑_(i = 1)^(8)(x_{i} - x^(―))(y_{i} - y^(―)) = 2.3$.\n\nThen, $S_{xy} =$\n{{field-1}}."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204008 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0afa4d8-6d02-52c6-9836-12089de8f406" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Sums of Squares Given a Dataset or Summary Statistics"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8486b33b-8bf0-5e6d-960f-e29d75f19ee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202601} {:answer/id #uuid "a2a49094-e92e-51ad-b4ef-48bf5522e974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202602} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f4a1dd-3e64-55e0-9acf-a0eb6e89892e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202603} {:answer/id #uuid "00339c52-281a-524c-b787-35cce57bcb66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202604} {:answer/id #uuid "559c7298-fc5d-52cf-b80d-f5486f92f4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S_{yy} = 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202605}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4c725d7d-b2fd-5e71-9b0d-3ba4a9496550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186202600}] :question/id #uuid "de5cf12f-ad3f-5f2c-aa7f-2181f5de72bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-251488" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $5$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$x_{i}$** | $5$ | $11$ | $9$ | $12$ | $18$ |\n| --- | ---: 